# Commit message — gitmoji conventions
# Format: <gitmoji> <type>(<scope>): <subject in present tense>  (#issue)
#
# Examples:
#   ✨ feat(tts): add dynamic batching of requests
#   🐛 fix(stt): fix realtime WebSocket passthrough
#   📝 docs: document environment variables
#   🐳 chore(docker): add the ROCm override
#   ✅ test(chunking): cover sentence boundaries
#
# Gitmoji reference: https://gitmoji.dev
# The .githooks/commit-msg hook checks that the subject starts with a gitmoji.
#
# --- Subject line below (delete these comments before saving) ---

